1. Definitions

   "Mining" means running the Software, modified or not, to search nonces for
   the Proxima network, alone or through a pool, for yourself or for others,
   including as a paid or commercial operation.

   "Another Miner" means any software other than the Software, or a derivative
   of the Software, whose purpose includes searching nonces or proofs of work
   for Proxima or any other network.

   "Commercial" means sold, licensed or rented for a fee, carrying a developer
   fee or similar built-in payment, bundled with a paid product or service, or
   offered as a service for payment.

   "Closed-source" means distributed, offered or run for third parties without
   making the complete corresponding source code available to every recipient
   under this license.

2. What you may do

   a. Run the Software for Mining, on any hardware, on any pool, for any purpose,
      with no fee and no permission needed.
   b. Copy and redistribute the Software, in source or binary form, unmodified,
      provided this license, the copyright notice and the NOTICE file travel
      with it.
   c. Modify the Software for your own Mining and study it freely.
   d. Distribute your modifications, provided the complete corresponding source
      is included, the modified work stays under this license, and your changes
      are marked as such.

3. What you may not do without written permission

